From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:18:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add personal/consumer (Teams-for-Life) account support

Under ENABLE_TEAMS_PERSONAL, make login and messaging work for personal
Microsoft (live.com) accounts next to the work/school path:

- Split OAuth and API routing by host so the consumer teams.live.com
  mt/beta endpoints get their own Bearer token; they reject the org one.
- Load the classic Skype contact roster for consumer accounts, which have
  no org self-details, and route consumer 1:1 chats through the Teams
  thread model (the legacy "8:<user>" peer form 404s there).
- Add a headless OAuth auth-code login and deliver device-code sign-in
  instructions as an IM on UIs without a notify UI.
- Persist the refresh token as the account password so later logins take
  the silent refresh path.
- Personal accounts get no real-time Trouter message push, so poll
  history on a timer, seed the poll cursor once so the window is not
  always empty, and dedup re-fetched messages by server id.
- Plumb a real error callback through teams_post_or_get_with_error(),
  cap the dedup cache, guard the poll against overlapping fetches, and
  make HTTP body logging opt-in (verbose + unsafe debug) since bodies
  carry names and tokens.

The plugin ids stay unchanged, and both can be overridden at build time.

This is the squashed state of the open upstream pull request #85, plus
the two fixes for the build errors reported in its review:
teams_mt_oauth_cb() is now only built with ENABLE_TEAMS_PERSONAL, and the
dedup cache uses g_hash_table_insert(), because g_hash_table_add() needs
GLib 2.32 and the Windows build uses 2.28.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/EionRobb/purple-teams/pull/85]
